{
  "name": "preview_retention_change",
  "description": "Preview how proposed EvidenceRetentionPolicy changes would shorten the retention of evidence already stored, before applying them through Kubernetes (ADR-240). Applies the proposal to the latest accepted policies of the hub (no source_cluster_id) or of one cluster's local source exactly as reconciliation will after acceptance, over all retained artifacts whose deletion is not yet due (one aggregate over the stored deadlines): affected artifacts per cluster and class, how many would become unreadable or due for deletion at once, and the earliest new access end and deletion dates. A longer limit never moves an already bound date. Artifacts for which a newly selected label selector would need historical labels are Unknown, never assumed; clusters whose policy source is not current are listed as incomplete. Groups and incomplete clusters are paged: repeat the same request with next_cursor. For fleet operators; it changes nothing: apply the change with kubectl or GitOps.",
  "transports": [
    "browser"
  ],
  "annotations": {
    "readOnlyHint": true,
    "destructiveHint": false,
    "openWorldHint": false
  },
  "inputSchema": {
